{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24049 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "Phlorofucofuroeckol A is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the CD70 antigen through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Phlorofucofuroeckol A directly targets DMS-79, which in turn is a target of 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, methyl ester, and subsequently of the CD70 antigen. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Phlorofucofuroeckol A may influence the expression or activity of CD70 antigen via the DMS-79 pathway. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CD70 antigen supports the idea that Phlorofucofuroeckol A could act as a modulator of CD70 antigen expression, potentially through the regulation of DMS-79. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular mechanisms involved, suggesting that Phlorofucofuroeckol A may play a role in the biological processes associated with CD70 antigen, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
